## Course overview

Spanish ab initio is a Standard Level language-acquisition course designed for **true beginners**. Over two years students build the ability to understand and communicate in Spanish about everyday topics, and gain insight into Spanish-speaking cultures.

## What you will study

The course covers five prescribed themes through practical, real-world language:

- **Identities**
- **Experiences**
- **Human ingenuity**
- **Social organisation**
- **Sharing the planet**

## Assessment

| Component | Weighting | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (productive writing) | 25% | Two written tasks |
| Paper 2 (listening & reading) | 50% | Receptive skills assessment |
| Individual Oral | 25% | Conversation based on a visual stimulus |

> Spanish ab initio is offered at **Standard Level only**, as defined by the IB.
